{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/worldmodule\/event"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"symbolKind":"protocol","modules":[{"name":"WorldModule"}],"title":"Event","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Event"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Event"}],"roleHeading":"Protocol","remoteSource":{"fileName":"Events.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/WorldModule\/Events.swift#L27"},"externalID":"s:11WorldModule5EventP"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Event"},"abstract":[{"text":"A type that describes a message one part of a program sends and other parts read later.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Sending Events","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Events","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/EventsView"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Sending-Events"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Event","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","text":"Sendable","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use events to decouple the code that notices something from the code that responds to it:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a physics step sends a collision, and separate damage and sound systems each read it. Declare","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an event as a type that conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", send it with ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/send(_:)"},{"text":", and read it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/readEvents(_:by:)"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["struct Collision: Event { var first: Entity, second: Entity }","enum DamageReader {}","","var world = World()","let ship = world.spawn(Health(current: 3))","let asteroid = world.spawn(Health(current: 1))","world.send(Collision(first: ship, second: asteroid))","","for collision in world.readEvents(Collision.self, by: DamageReader.self) {","    world[Health.self, of: collision.first].current -= 1","}","print(world[Health.self, of: ship])","\/\/ Prints \"Health(current: 2)\""],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Events wait in the world’s "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Events","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" resource until "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/updateEvents()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" drops them,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so senders and readers don’t need to run at the same moment. Unlike an "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/EntityEvent","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event isn’t aimed at an entity and runs no code when sent."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"inheritsFrom","title":"Inherits From","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships"},{"type":"conformingTypes","title":"Conforming Types","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/